{
  "_comment": "Canonical registry of every CLI subcommand exposed by `brainstorm` / `storm`. Keys are `<receiver>:<verb>` where receiver is `program` (top-level) or a `<group>Cmd` variable (routerCmd, vaultCmd, etc.) defined in packages/cli/src/bin/brainstorm.ts. The contract-check gate at scripts/contract-checks/cli-subcommand-registry.mjs walks the CLI source, extracts every .command() call with its receiver context, and fails the build if (a) a new entry shows up in source but isn't registered here, or (b) a registered entry has no source declaration. The Stage-3 review caught that the original leaf-keyed registry deduped 99 source declarations to 77 entries \u2014 `vault delete` would have passed silently because `delete` was already registered against a different group. Group-prefixed keys make subcommand drift inside a group visible.",
  "_categories": {
    "tool-driven": "Backed by a defineTool() entry \u2014 the verb is the CLI alias for a tool.",
    "contract-driven": "Backed by a platform contract endpoint \u2014 the verb is a CLI dispatcher for the HTTP surface.",
    "infrastructure": "Session/config/vault/projects/etc. \u2014 operator-level commands with no tool/contract counterpart.",
    "agent-loop": "The chat REPL, agent dispatch, plan mode, orchestration \u2014 the core interactive surface.",
    "ecosystem": "Manage the brainstorm ecosystem itself \u2014 onboarding, peers, sync, setup."
  },
